.SH NAME
sqrail \- run bounded read-only SQL over local files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sqrail
.B schema
[\fB--memory\fR \fISIZE\fR] [\fB--threads\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--timeout\fR \fIDURATION\fR] [\fB--max-input-files\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--strict-schema\fR] \fIFILE\fR...
.br
.B sqrail
.B check
[\fB-t\fR \fINAME=PATH\fR]... [\fB--memory\fR \fISIZE\fR] [\fB--threads\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--timeout\fR \fIDURATION\fR] [\fB--max-rows\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--max-input-files\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--max-sql-bytes\fR \fISIZE\fR] [\fB--strict-schema\fR] [\fISQL\fR|\fB-\fR]
.br
.B sqrail
.B run
[\fB-t\fR \fINAME=PATH\fR]... [\fB-o\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB--memory\fR \fISIZE\fR] [\fB--threads\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--spill\fR \fIDIR\fR [\fB--max-spill\fR \fISIZE\fR]] [\fB--timeout\fR \fIDURATION\fR] [\fB--max-rows\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--max-output-bytes\fR \fISIZE\fR] [\fB--max-input-files\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--max-sql-bytes\fR \fISIZE\fR] [\fB--stats\fR] [\fB--strict-schema\fR] [\fISQL\fR|\fB-\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
sqrail executes one read-only SQL query over explicitly bound local CSV, TSV,
JSON, or Parquet inputs. It provides three commands: schema discovers names and
types, check validates bindings and returns a plan without execution, and run
executes once and emits JSONL or an explicitly selected output file.
.PP
Resource limits fail closed. Diagnostics are one JSON object on standard error.
Output files are private, committed atomically, and never overwrite an existing
path. Run
.B sqrail --help
for the complete operational contract.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
The command completed successfully.
.TP
.B 2
The command line, limits, or input SQL form was invalid.
.TP
.B 3
An input path, schema, or file format was invalid.
.TP
.B 4
SQL parsing, binding, planning, execution, or a result limit failed.
.TP
.B 5
An output path, format, write, or byte limit failed.
.TP
.B 70
An internal error occurred.
.SH FILES
sqrail reads no configuration file. Inputs are available to SQL only through explicit
.B -t
bindings. A spill directory is used only when explicitly selected with
.BR --spill .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
  sqrail schema sales.csv
  sqrail run -t sales=sales.csv 'SELECT count(*) AS n FROM sales'
  sqrail run -t sales=sales.csv -o result.parquet - < query.sql
.fi
